"""research-runner.py - runs the deep-research jobs that Jan (tools/research-mcp.py) queues (2026-10-17).

Runs as the systemd user service deep-research-runner.service. One job at a time, in the order they were asked;
everything is on disk (jobs/<id>/job.json), so jobs survive a restart of the runner, LDR or the PC.

  start      Strata on demand (strata-compare's strata-ensure.sh: "Starting Strata..."), LDR + strata-proxy + LDR's
             SearXNG (run-ldr.sh start), the job's settings for the deep patch (run/next-research.json: research
             time, files, seed), then LDR's /api/start_research. Not while a test holds strata-compare's measurement
             lock, and not during the night pause (a queued job waits).
  run        pause / resume / cancel / yield / night pause go to the proxy gate through run/research-control.json:
             the gate holds the research between model calls and stops the research clock (run/research-clock.json).
  finish     the deep report (results/deep-runs/research-<rid>/report.md) is copied to reports/<date>-<slug>.md with
             a header, plus an .html copy; a desktop notification. Failures notify too.
  interrupt  if LDR is gone while a job runs (the PC was off, LDR restarted), the job continues as a new run seeded
             from the earlier runs' evidence and notes, with the research time that is left.
  memory     MemAvailable below 12 GB stops the research (the standing floor since 2026-10-19 evening; 16 / 20 before) and reports the lowest value.
  paid run   (10-29, item 7) run/paid-run.json {"kind": "research", "run": <job id>} while a job's research is in LDR, so
             the paid-search budget counts LDR's searches as that research (tools/ldr_runfiles.py); removed at the end.
  stamps     LDR is restarted when a run/ldr.* stamp does not fit the job - since 10-29 also run/ldr.modelprofile
             (LDR_MODEL_PROFILE, default flash-next; the profile's name and file hash).

Settings: research.conf (read every few seconds). Log: logs/research-runner.log.
"""
